=====================================================================
ITEM 4 - Is 24.2% honest?
=====================================================================
It counts: test functions in tests/ and .agent-pipeline/03_e2e_suites that carry all
three markers (test_id, requirements, scenario) - 480 of 1984 discovered functions.
It omits: (a) whether those markers point at anything real - the runner reports 750
unresolved spec references, i.e. markers that exist but name an id in no spec file, so
"compliant" means marker-presence, not traceability to a requirement; (b) 120 files with
noncompliant tests; (c) the fact that enforcement_scope is delta_only_plus_artifact_ratchet,
so the gate fails only when markers are LOST against the recorded commit - adding new
unmarked tests raises the denominator and lowers 24.2% without failing anything.
One line: 24.2% is an accurate count of marker presence but reads as "24.2% of
requirements are traced and protected", which is not what it measures and not what the
gate enforces. I did not run a mutation adding an unmarked test to prove (c) - not
attempted, budget.

